          "adms:versionNotes": "WS-1 VOCABULARY CONSOLIDATION, lot 1i. owl:imports written as plain strings (JSON-LD literals: no reasoner followed them, so this file was reasoned in isolation and the apex declarations of M3_GrammarFoundation were invisible to it) rewritten as IRIs {\"@id\": ...}: 3 import(s). Target = the imported file's document URL, resolved by @base (Michel, 2026-09-30: aligning ontology IRIs with document URLs is recorded as a later lot). Triage: ontology/docs/_01_Worksite/WS-1/WS-1_FamilyA_Triage.md."
        },
        {
          "owl:versionInfo": "1.3.0",
          "dcterms:date": "2026-09-30",
          "adms:versionNotes": "WS-1 VOCABULARY CONSOLIDATION, lot 1e. Changelog container m2:changelog -> m3:changelog (the owl:AnnotationProperty declared in M3_GrammarFoundation); entry keys version/date/changes -> owl:versionInfo / dcterms:date / adms:versionNotes (ADMS accepted, Michel 2026-09-30); prefix adms declared. Previously the whole changelog was dropped on JSON-LD expansion."
        }
      ],
      "m0:vsmPrinciples": {
        "viability": "Capacity to maintain separate existence through adaptation",
        "recursion": "Every viable system contains viable subsystems with complete S1-S5 structure",
        "requisiteVariety": "V(Regulator) ≥ V(Disturbance) (Ashby)",
        "autonomy": "Maximum S1 freedom compatible with systemic cohesion"
      },
      "m0:architecture": {
        "S1": "Operations — primary activities, autonomous units, direct environment interface",
        "S2": "Coordination — anti-oscillatory, prevents inter-S1 conflicts",
        "S3": "Optimization (inside/now) — resource allocation, performance monitoring, S3* audit",
        "S4": "Intelligence (outside/then) — strategic scanning, future adaptation",
        "S5": "Policy (identity/ethos) — ultimate authority, arbitrates S3-S4 conflicts"
      },
      "dcterms:source": {
        "primary": "Stafford Beer, Brain of the Firm (1972)",
        "secondary": [
          "Beer, Heart of Enterprise (1979)",
          "Beer, Diagnosing the System (1985)"
        ]
      },
